## Progress

- 2026-10-26 21:03 UTC: Goal written from the owner's words. Lane 9 of the audit reviews the roles.
- 2026-10-26 23:16 UTC: Every role's fixed texts are in `src/agents/roles/`, one module for each role, with `index.ts` as the table of the 15 roles (what each does, where it runs, its model and programs, whether the owner's messages reach it, and its texts). The tools' names and the research tools are in `src/agents/tools/`, and the paper's parts in `core`. A golden test holds every text byte for byte, written before the move and unchanged by it; a second test fails when a role module exports a text the table leaves out. The site's [Agent roles](../../_site/src/content/docs/reference/agent-roles.md) page is written from the table (`npm run docs:agents`), and the docs check holds them equal. Still to do: each role's assembly for a run as one function with no side effects, the record of every prompt sent, and the dashboard, REST, MCP and command line.
- 2026-10-27 19:38 UTC: Golden tests of every role's prompt today (goal 125's step 4): `tests/agents/prompts.test.ts` captures what each of the 15 roles' models is sent in Pi for a sample run, where it is sent (the scheduler, the trial, the supervisor's round against the harness's API, the summary call, the model check), and holds the system text, the first message and the tools in `tests/agents/golden/prompts/`, with what differs between runs as placeholders (ids, commits, times, paths, ports, what the judge measured, the model check's word). Each role is found by the role whose text its system text starts with. Still to capture: the variants in the other programs (the worker in OpenCode, Claude Code and Codex, the planners and the advisors run as programs), which take each program's stand-in; then the program table, with every prompt by standard input.

